+/**
+ * Process-wide singleton "owner" wrapper around pimSFXLoop, the install step
+ * that runs self-extracting-executable (SFX) installer payloads. One of 7
+ * near-identical Loop-owner wrapper singletons in pim_core. Structurally
+ * almost identical to pimMSICopier -- per this class's own header comment,
+ * "the self extracting executable is possibly running an MSI installer, so
+ * we ensure we are not also running an MSI installer."
+ *
+ * Locking contract: gated by the SAME external pimOKToRunMsiexec()/
+ * pimFreeMsiexec() functions (pim_util) that pimMSICopier uses -- not an
+ * independent mutex. Consequence: at most one of {an MSI install via
+ * pimMSICopier, an SFX install via this class} can be in flight
+ * process-wide at any moment; see pimMSICopier.h for the full mechanism
+ * (an in-process mutex plus a Windows Installer registry-key probe).
+ *
+ * Unlike pimCopier/pimShortcuts/pimRegEdit/pimServices/pimDownloader,
+ * Status() takes no output parameters -- no percent-complete or
+ * time-remaining is reported for SFX installs. Like pimMSICopier, Status()'s
+ * "done" branch does NOT delete the owned pimSFXLoop or release the gate --
+ * cleanup is caller-driven via Release()/Kill().
+ *
+ * Sole caller in this codebase: pimEntitlement.
+ */
 class pimSFXCopier
 {
 private:
